# EOL policy — the fix for the "passes on one checkout, SyntaxError on another" class (F-054/F-060).
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` and had NO .gitattributes, so every
# file was stored LF in the object database but materialised CRLF in the working tree. `git status`
# stays clean either way (autocrlf normalises CRLF back to LF on the way in), which makes the
# difference INVISIBLE to git — two worktrees at the SAME sha could disagree about the bytes on disk.
#
# That is not cosmetic for `.mjs`. Vite/vitest does not run its esbuild transform over `.mjs`, and
# its shebang strip does not survive a CRLF line ending, so an executable module whose first line is
#
#     #!/usr/bin/env node\r\n
#
# fails to parse the moment any vitest test imports it:
#
#     SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token
#
# reported at COLLECT time against the *importing* test file (0 tests collected), not against the
# .mjs itself. With LF the identical file parses fine. All 9 shebang-bearing files in this repo are
# `.mjs`, so pinning that extension covers the whole class.
#
# Pinned deliberately narrowly: a blanket `* text=auto eol=lf` would renormalise the entire working
# tree in one commit. Widen only with a dedicated, measured commit.
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed by sh/bash; a CR is a syntax error there too.
*.sh text eol=lf
